1
00:00:00,421 --> 00:00:03,051
(Mrs Cooper:)You know, we have an Indian gentleman
at our church.

2
00:00:03,216 --> 00:00:05,466
(Mrs Cooper:)A Dr. Patel. It's a beautiful story.

3
00:00:05,635 --> 00:00:10,015
(Mrs Cooper:)The Lord spoke to him and moved him
to give us all 20 percent off on LASEK.

4
00:00:10,181 --> 00:00:12,101
(Mrs Cooper:)You know, those that needed it.

5
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:14,557
(Leonard:)That is a lovely story.

6
00:00:14,727 --> 00:00:16,477
Are we gonna do anything
about Sheldon?

7
00:00:16,646 --> 00:00:19,186
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, we will.
You have to take your time with Sheldon.

8
00:00:19,357 --> 00:00:21,527
His father, God rest his soul, used to say:

9
00:00:21,692 --> 00:00:24,902
"Mary, you have to take your time
with Sheldon."

10
00:00:25,738 --> 00:00:28,578
- Sounds like a wise man.
- Oh, not so wise.

11
00:00:28,741 --> 00:00:31,831
He once tried to fight a bobcat
for some licorice.

12
00:00:32,703 --> 00:00:38,253
(Mrs Cooper:)So everybody grab a plate
and a pretty placemat that Shelly wove.

13
00:00:38,417 --> 00:00:40,757
(Penny:)Has Shelly ever freaked out
like this before?

14
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:41,960
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, all the time.

15
00:00:42,129 --> 00:00:44,339
(Mrs Cooper:)I remember one summer
when he was 13...

16
00:00:44,507 --> 00:00:47,637
(Mrs Cooper:)...he built a small nuclear reactor
in the shed...

17
00:00:47,802 --> 00:00:50,932
...and told everybody he was gonna provide
electricity for the town.

18
00:00:51,097 --> 00:00:56,027
(Mrs Cooper:)Well, the only problem was, he had no,
what you call, fissionable materials.

